message.content:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The user reported that Tui's overlay (an HTML/Tauri game overlay in `/app`) is stuck on the menu: "picking a game never actually launches a run, and the window chrome around the board is dead too, so the minimize-to-pill button, the resize toggle, the How to Play guide and the sign-out confirmation all do nothing."

   Their explicit ask, verbatim: *"Wire the whole session back up: starting a run, pausing when the agent needs you and resuming, restarting mid-run, and ending a shift cleanly, plus the window minimize/restore/resize behavior the README and the on-screen buttons describe, including saving progress so a run can resume on the next launch."*

   Deliverable: the full session lifecycle — start a run (menu → variations → play, deep links `?game=`, host `gamepigeon:launch`), pause on agent-stop and resume, restart mid-run, end a shift cleanly back to the menu, window minimize-to-pill / restore / compact↔expanded resize, the How to Play dialog, the sign-out confirmation dialog, and localStorage save/resume of a run.

   This was the ONLY user turn in the conversation. No corrections or additional feedback were ever given. No security constraints, forbidden files, or credential-handling rules were stated by the user.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Bun 1.3.11 workspace (`@tui-games/tui`); `bun x tsc` for typecheck (`npx`/`node` are NOT available in this environment)
   - Tauri v2 shell (`tauri/src/main.rs`) + browser preview mode (`overlay/preview.html`, `scripts/preview-overlay.ts`)
   - Host→webview events via Rust `window.eval`: `gamepigeon:launch` (`{game, variation}`), `gamepigeon:pause`, `gamepigeon:resume`, `gamepigeon:reset`, `gamepigeon:auth-success` (`{email}` only — no id), `gamepigeon:auth-error`, `gamepigeon:sync-error`, `gamepigeon:sync-success`, `gamepigeon:worker-budget`
   - Tauri commands used: `shutdown`, `read_settings`, `write_settings`, `read_local_scores`, `append_local_score`, `queue_recording_chunks`, `read_auth_session`, `read_sync_error`, `sign_out`, `start_auth_login`, `cancel_auth_login`, `read_worker_model_config`, `complete_worker_model`, `cancel_worker_model`, `record_analytics_event`, `read_update_flag`
   - `LocalScoreInput` Rust struct has NO `serde(rename_all)` → JS must send snake_case (`game_id`, `game_type`, `variation_id`, `score`, `success`, `completed_at`, `duration_ms`, `platform`); `game_id` must match `safe_recording_id(_, "game_")`, `completed_at` must end with `Z` and be ≤40 chars, `platform` must be `"terminal"|"overlay"`
   - `EpisodeEndReason` union (from `@tui-games/trace-export`): `game_over|won|lost|user_quit|restart|timeout|client_closed|engine_error`
   - `captureOverlayEvent` `EventData` union: `{app_version, platform}` | `{game_type, variation_id}` | `{game_type, variation_id, outcome:"completed"|"abandoned", score, success, duration_ms, actions_taken}`
   - Phaser 3 canvas scene (`mountRestaurantArenaScene`) with `onUi: (action:"menu"|"restart"|"help") => void`
   - `WorkerOrchestrator` steps the engine itself (`game.step("tick")`, `game.stepEnvelope`), bypassing `stepGame`; `start()` doubles as resume; `pause()` aborts in-flight requests
   - `RestaurantGame.tickMs()` returns 0 when the sim is unstarted/paused/on an open decision/over — the single gate for both schedulers
   - Arena keymap: `space→sim_toggle, t→tick, f→sim_speed, p, v, 1/2/3, o, h→hold_seating, n→pass_round` (no `r`, so `r` is free for restart); arena variation ids are `tutorial-shift`, `dinner-rush`, `quiet-tuesday`, `saturday-night` (no `classic`, so Rust's default `"classic"` falls back to index 0)
   - Arena tick cadence: `BASE_TICK_MS = 3000`, tutorial-shift override `tickMs: 4500`, `SIM_SPEEDS = [1, 2, 4]`
   - TS config: root `tsconfig.json` (strict, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, includes only `src/**/*` + `scripts/overlay.ts`); `overlay/tsconfig.json` extends it with DOM libs, `types:["bun"]`, `include: ["./**/*.ts"]`
   - `happy-dom` is available in node_modules but provides no real 2D canvas context, so Phaser cannot be loaded under it

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   - **`/app/overlay/app.ts`** (now ~2045 lines) — the main file. All session wiring was written here this session.

     *Imports added:*
     ```ts
     import { FEATURED_GAME_IDS, MENU_GAMES, findGame, isPlayable } from "../src/games/registry.js";
     // ...
     import { clearSavedGame, loadSavedGame, restoreGame, saveGame, type SavedGame } from "./persistence.js";
     import {
       RUNNING as CLOCK_RUNNING,
       type PauseState,
       type PauseTrigger,
       pausePromptTitle,
       pausedFor,
       shouldPauseForAgent,
       showsPausePrompt,
     } from "./pause-state.js";
     ```
     plus `clearSignInPending`, `setSignInStatus`, `signOut` added to the `./auth.js` import, and `MIN_SIZE`, `PILL_SIZE`, `applyOverlaySize`, `floorSize` to the `./tauri-bridge.js` import.

     *`browserKey` gained:*
     ```ts
     // README documents `Esc` and `q` as the same gesture, so they arrive here
     // as the same key rather than being special-cased at every screen.
     case "Escape": return "quit";
     ```

     *New module state:*
     ```ts
     let pauseState: PauseState = CLOCK_RUNNING;
     let windowMode: "floor" | "pill" = "floor";
     let tickTimer: number | undefined;
     let runSeed = 0;
     let runVariationId = "";
     let runActions: string[] = [];
     let pendingLaunch: { gameId: string; variationId?: string } | undefined;
     ```

     *`saveSetting` now applies the frame live:*
     ```ts
     if (key === "defaultWindowSize") {
       expanded = settings.defaultWindowSize === "expanded";
       renderResizeButton();
       applyWindowSize();
     }
     ```

     *Window chrome:*
     ```ts
     function applyWindowSize(center = false): void {
       const pill = windowMode === "pill";
       const target = pill ? PILL_SIZE : floorSize(expanded ? "expanded" : "compact");
       void applyOverlaySize(target, pill ? PILL_SIZE : MIN_SIZE)
         .then(() => (center ? windowHandle.center() : undefined))
         .catch(() => {});
     }
     function renderResizeButton(): void { /* textContent ↙/↗, aria-label Compact/Expand overlay */ }
     function toggleWindowSize(): void { if (windowMode === "pill") { restoreFromPill(); return; } expanded = !expanded; renderResizeButton(); applyWindowSize(); }
     function minimizeToPill(): void {
       pauseRun("minimized");
       windowMode = "pill";
       document.body.dataset.mode = "pill";
       applyWindowSize();
       document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("#pill")?.focus();
     }
     function restoreFromPill(): void {
       if (windowMode !== "pill") return;
       windowMode = "floor";
       delete document.body.dataset.mode;
       expanded = false;                // README: restore is always compact
       renderResizeButton();
       applyWindowSize();
       if (pauseState.trigger === "minimized") resumeRun();
       else scheduleClock();
     }
     async function shutdownOverlay(): Promise<void> { parkRunForRecovery(); await invoke("shutdown").catch(() => undefined); }
     function parkRunForRecovery(): void { persistRun(); if (activeTrace) flushSealedTrace(activeTrace); }
     const PILL_DRAG_THRESHOLD_PX = 4;
     function bindPill(): void { /* pointerdown records origin; pointermove past threshold sets dragged + startDragging(); click restores unless dragged */ }
     ```

     *Dialogs:*
     ```ts
     type Dialog = "pause" | "how-to-play" | "signout";
     const DIALOGS: Readonly<Record<Dialog, string>> = {
       pause: "#return-prompt", "how-to-play": "#how-to-play", signout: "#signout-prompt",
     };
     let dialog: Dialog | null = null;
     let howToPlayReturnsToPause = false;
     function setDialog(next: Dialog | null): void {
       dialog = next;
       for (const name of Object.keys(DIALOGS) as Dialog[]) {
         const el = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(DIALOGS[name]);
         if (el) el.hidden = name !== next;
       }
       if (next === "pause") { const t = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#return-title"); if (t) t.textContent = pausePromptTitle(pauseState); }
       if (next === "signout") setSignOutError(null);
       if (next) document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(`${DIALOGS[next]} .primary`)?.focus();
     }
     function closeDialog(): void { setDialog(null); scheduleClock(); }
